WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.730
- I'm here with the very
funny Ricky Gervais,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.140
who I just learned was, once upon a time,

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.040
also a budding rock star.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.560
Okay, so can you explain this photo to me?

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.820
- All I can say is, I was 20 years old.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.007
Look at that!
- Sexy.

00:00:15.007 --> 00:00:18.949
- And I think when (laughs),

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:21.400
if I look at that, people
think I'm embarrassed

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.540
about how I looked then.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.540
No, I'm embarrassed about how I look now.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.881
- I would never be embarrassed

00:00:27.881 --> 00:00:28.714
about how you looked then!

00:00:28.714 --> 00:00:30.508
You looked like a frigin' rockstar!

00:00:30.508 --> 00:00:33.690
- (laughs) And people
say, "What happened?"

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.180
I'll tell you what happened,

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.370
beer and pizza, that's what happened,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.663
and I don't regret one,
I don't regret one.

00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:42.180
- [Kelly] That's like
people always attack me.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.400
They're like, "What has she been doin?"

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.680
Well, obviously, eating and
not working out. (laughs)

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.870
I'm like, "It doesn't
take a rocket scientist

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.020
to figure out someone
just maybe has a glass

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.853
of wine every night,

00:00:51.853 --> 00:00:54.061
and is like, 'No, I won't
go to the gym.'" (laughs)

00:00:54.061 --> 00:00:57.610
- No, and people say,
"Oh, if you gave up beer

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.060
and pizza, you'd live longer."

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.400
But I only wanna live
longer to eat more pizza

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.810
and drink more beer.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.063
- Is it real living, is the question.

00:01:06.063 --> 00:01:08.400
- Exactly, yeah!
(Both laughing)

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.920
- All right, and so, how did
you get started in music?

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.753
I didn't know that like,

00:01:11.753 --> 00:01:13.040
is that your first love?

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:13.873
- I guess so.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:18.740
I mean, growing up I
loved science and nature,

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.320
and then when maybe 13, 14
and I've got into music.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.140
And then when I was a teenager
I discovered David Bowie,

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.370
and then I went to university

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.730
and I actually did sciences.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.380
I got into university to study sciences,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.370
but then I realized, no,
I want to join a band.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:36.660
I've come to university to join a band

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.210
and I changed to philosophy,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:42.099
which was a lot less
hours a week than science.

00:01:42.099 --> 00:01:43.023
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:43.023 --> 00:01:44.695
- One's an easier degree.

00:01:44.695 --> 00:01:48.150
- (laughs) Yeah, the rock star's degree.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.840
And I started a band

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.620
and we got signed, and it was
over as quick as it started.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.560
My rock career was one year,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.120
one year long. (laughs)

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.820
- [Kelly] Hey, that's longer
than some people get, so.

